Hide official plugins listed in PASEO_ZCODE_SUPPRESSED_PLUGINS

Purpose: paseo-plugin-zcode-provider (ADR 19) runs ZCode in a standalone
Server that shares ~/.zcode with ZCode Desktop. Computer Use cannot start its
Helper there and Browser Use has no browser, yet the skills that Desktop
installed are still offered to the model. The provider lists such plugin IDs,
comma-separated, in PASEO_ZCODE_SUPPRESSED_PLUGINS. Plugin discovery and the
enabled plugins of an open session then skip them the same way they skip
suppressedBuiltins, without writing any configuration.

Target: the two places that apply suppressedBuiltins to official plugins in
ZCode a4b4445141eb7d3b3e99eada9292775383bfc44e:
- NodePluginAdapter.discoverPluginsSync in
  apps/zcode-cli/packages/adapters/src/plugins/index.ts, which every plugin
  discovery path uses;
- readEnabledPlugins in
  apps/zcode-cli/packages/adapters/src/plugins/live-inventory.ts (4.0), from
  which an open session's skill catalog and MCP configuration read the
  official plugins listed in the bundled marketplace partition. It has no
  discovery request, so it reads the Agent process's environment, which the
  Server passes on.

Remove when: ZCode offers an official per-process way to hide official
plugins, for example when ZCODE_CUA_PRODUCT_HELPER=0 hides cached
computer-use as resolveOfficialPluginRoots says it should.

